From ddddaf982d530f2de81ab0c48009290cdc727c06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilan Joselevich <personal@ilanjoselevich.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:27:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] workers: report each running build's phase, and show it
 to watchers

The scheduler sees assignments, not build starts. A derivation stays
"assigned" through the client's upload, input fetching, the build and
publishing. A dashboard that says "Running" or names the current phase
needs what only the builder knows.

Builders note when each build started on the nix-daemon and its last
stdenv phase with the time it began. Their WorkerReport lists the
running builds that changed since the last report, and every running
build in a session's first report, under the existing rules: at most
every 2 s, only when something changed, only after ReportsWanted. A
buildCommand build, a NixOS test included, never sets a phase and
reports its start alone.

The scheduler keeps the three values on the assigned entry, for that
worker's current assignment only. Once a second it sends a DrvState
with the new CAUSE_PROGRESS for each derivation a report changed.
DrvState gains build_phase, build_started_ms and
build_phase_started_ms, set in snapshots too. Both sides cut a phase
name to 64 bytes and make it valid UTF-8, since a report that is not
would fail to parse and drop the builder's session.

events-test and builder-log-test cover the reports, the DrvStates, stale
assignments, requeues, and long or invalid phase names.
